  <data name="CommandlineHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This is a list of the possible commands for the command line, with the necessary syntax.\par
The words in {\i italics} have to be substitued with whatever you want to use.\par
The parts in [square brackets] are optional.\par
For {\i text}, you can use the name of a translation of the Bible or collection of notes (and only in that case you 
have to correctly type the upper and lower case letters) or the abbreviation of a translation or collection. If one 
is not given, the last translation is used (the one at the bottom right of the main window of the programma).\par
If there is a space in the phrase, passage or text, you need to put it between "inverted commas".\par
You can put several commands in one line, separating them with a semi-colon.\par
\par
search {\i phrase} [in {\i passage}] [from {\i text}]\par
show {\i passage} [from {\i text}]\par
show {\i passage} from bibles\par
show {\i passage} from commentaries\par
copy {\i passage} [from {\i text}]\par
concordance {\i passage} [from {\i text}]\par
similar {\i passage} [from {\i Bible}]\par
definitions {\i passage} [from {\i text}]\par
note {\i passage} from {\i collection}\par
note {\i title} from {\i collection}\par
copynote {\i passage} from {\i collection}\par
copynote {\i title} from {\i collection}\par
references {\i passage} from {\i collection}\par
view [{\i passage}] [from {\i text}]\par
view [{\i passage}] [from {\i parallel texts}]\par
goto {\i passage}\par
open {\i file_name}\par
info {\i phrase}\par
info {\i passage}\par
link {\i address/program} [{\i parameters}]\par
close [all]\par
update [existing][all]\par
set bible {\i Bible_name}\par
set language {\i italiano or english or español}\par
help\par
?\par
\par
For example:\par
search abba in rom-ebr from "American Standard Version"; note amos from "Enciclopedia biblica"; concordance "Mt 1-14" from acv\par</value>
  </data>
